THOUGHT: The NullAway error occurs because `getInstance()` is declared non-null but returns `holder`, which is annotated `@Nullable`. The simplest localized fix is to enforce non-null before returning, throwing an exception if `initialize` was never called; this preserves the non-null contract without changing other APIs. I’ll update `getInstance()` accordingly, then run the prescribed Gradle command to ensure the error is gone and no syntax issues were introduced.

```bash
cd /home/joos/projects/nullrepair/nullness-benchmarks/eureka && sed -i '44,46c\  public static EurekaServerContextHolder getInstance() {
    if (holder == null) {
      throw new IllegalStateException("EurekaServerContextHolder is not initialized");
    }
    return holder;
  }' eureka-core/src/main/java/com/netflix/eureka/EurekaServerContextHolder.java && nl -ba eureka-core/src/main/java/com/netflix/eureka/EurekaServerContextHolder.java | sed -n '34,60p' && ./gradlew eureka-core:compileJava -x test -q > build_output.log 2>&1 || grep -A 5 -B 5 'EurekaServerContextHolder.java' build_output.log
```

